<title>FINLAND: Tamro to sell Novartis drugs in Sweden.</title>
<headline>Tamro to sell Novartis drugs in Sweden.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish pharmaceuticals wholesaler Tamro Oy said in a statement on Wednesday it had expanded its agreement with Swiss Novartis to include distribution in Sweden.</p>
<p>It said Novartis was the world's second largest pharmaceuticals producer and that the agreement was important since Novartis was the first large manufacturer to use Tamro's model for distribution in the Nordic area.</p>
<p>Novartis' 1996 net sales in Sweden totalled about 479 million markka, Tamro said, adding its own total net sales last year were 13.2 billion markka.</p>
</text>
